    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That looks good. Can you dive a bit deeper into the 'Automated Testing' and 'Staging' gates? Specifically, I'm worried about things slipping through the cracks or unexpected errors bypassing the security scans. How do we make the gates \"tighter\" so nothing unverified gets through to the next stage?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To tighten the **Automated Testing** gate, implement strict code coverage thresholds (e.g., 85% minimum) and mandatory static application security testing ($\\text{SAST}$) to proactively find vulnerabilities like SQL injection. For **Staging**, mandate that the environment mirrors production exactly and require successful execution of complex, real-user workflow simulations before promotion. This layered approach minimizes the chance of unverified or vulnerable code progressing further down the pipeline.",
      "source": "target",
